  pair_between(/0|[1-9]\d*/, ".", /0|[1-9]\d*/, 1, 4, 1, 10)   (versions 1.4 to 1.10)
    '1.4'        -> accept 
    '1.9'        -> accept 
    '1.10'       -> accept 
    '1.3'        -> reject 
    '1.11'       -> reject 
    '2.0'        -> reject 
    '0.9'        -> reject 
    '1.04'       -> reject 
    '1x4'        -> reject 
  pair_between(/\d+/, ".", /\d+/, 1, 4, 1, 10)   (the same with \d+ fields: padded reads 1.04 as 1.4)
    '1.04'       -> accept 
    '01.10'      -> accept 
    '1.010'      -> accept 
    '1.011'      -> reject 
  contrast: the separator as rx text /./ instead of the string "." (accepts 1x4)
    '1.4'        -> accept 
    '1x4'        -> accept 
    contrast: a STRING range between("1.4", "1.10") (the language's string order, Python str compare): "1.4" <= "1.10" is False -> the set is EMPTY; and between("1.4", "1.9") accepts ['1.4', '1.5', '1.9', '1.45']
